%% DM26-0670

%% A pod restarts in place, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/deployments.md, steps 4 and 5). How a workload asks for its certificates is
%% general/workload_certificate_issuance, how it ends is general/shutdown_pipeline, and what it asks for once it has registered is general/configuration_replay.
%% The credentials agent's own restart has a ticket besides: general/core_restart_ticket.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Kubelet
    participant Agent as workload container
    participant Daemon as custody daemon<br/>(a native sidecar)
    participant Init as polar-init<br/>(init container)
    participant CA as credentials agent

    Note over Kubelet,Agent: A Deployment of one, Recreate.<br/>The workload container is restartPolicy Always, with one rule:<br/>RestartAllContainers on every exit (NotIn nothing).

    Agent->>Agent: ends: a rejuvenation, a verdict or a signal through<br/>the shutdown pipeline, or a crash
    Agent-->>Kubelet: exit non-zero, its last log lines as its termination message
    Kubelet->>Kubelet: the rule matches.<br/>Same UID, IP and volumes.<br/>Each container's log<br/>goes with it
    Kubelet->>Daemon: stopped. The keys it held were only in its memory
    Kubelet->>Daemon: started again, empty
    Kubelet->>Init: started again
    Init->>Daemon: new keys, and a CSR for each
    Init->>CA: its certificates, asked for as at the pod's first start
    alt this pod was given one of that type within five minutes
        CA-->>Init: TooSoon, which is temporary, so polar-init waits it out
    else
        CA-->>Init: a new certificate
        CA->>CA: the old one is superseded,<br/>and published as revoked
    end
    Init->>Init: leave the one-use start marker (POLAR_INIT_START_MARKER)
    Init-->>Kubelet: exit 0
    Kubelet->>Agent: started
    Agent->>Agent: take the marker (POLAR_START_MARKER), before anything else starts
    Note over Agent: Then as at any start: configuration_startup,<br/>and the signed documents again

    alt the liveness probe killed the process (it was wedged)
        Note over Kubelet,Agent: The rule does not act on a liveness kill,<br/>so this container restarts alone,<br/>without polar-init
        Kubelet->>Agent: started, alone
        Agent->>Agent: no marker to take: "restarted without polar-init"
        Agent-->>Kubelet: exit 1, which the rule does act on: the whole pod restarts, from step 3
    end

    Note over Kubelet,CA: A pod with no custody daemon (the scheduler observer, whose git reads its key from a file) has its key on a volume, which outlives the restart.<br/>polar-init keeps a bundle that is still valid and asks only when it is not. The rest is the same.
